{"qid":"Q817","names":["Kuwait","State of Kuwait"],"title":"Kuwait","endonym":{"native":"الكويت","lang":"ar"},"capsule":"Kuwait emerged as a distinct polity in the mid-18th century when the Bani Utbah federation settled the site and around 1752 elected Sabah I bin Jaber as their first ruler, founding the Al-Sabah dynasty. In 1899 Mubarak the Great signed an exclusive agreement placing Kuwait's foreign relations under British protection, a status that shielded it from Ottoman absorption. Oil production from 1946 transformed Kuwait into the Persian Gulf's largest exporter within a decade, and full independence was declared on 19 June 1961, making it the first Gulf state to adopt a written constitution and an elected parliament.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Post-1899 boundaries are well attested through British imperial treaties and modern international agreements; pre-protectorate limits of Al-Sabah authority are less precisely defined.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: History of Kuwait","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_Kuwait"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Kuwait","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kuwait"},{"label":"Britannica: Kuwait","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Kuwait"}],"britannica":"place/Kuwait","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Kuwait","rulers":[{"qid":"Q26922","name":"Sabah I bin Jaber","start":1752,"end":1776,"image":null,"nativeName":"صباح الأول بن جابر الصباح","nativeLang":"ar"},{"qid":"Q3269513","name":"Abdullah I Al-Sabah","start":1763,"end":1814,"image":null,"nativeName":"عبد الله بن صباح بن جابر الصباح","nativeLang":"ar"},{"qid":"Q888268","name":"Jaber I Al